.TH JELLYFIN-HOTCACHE 8 "September 2026" "jellyfin-hotcache 1.0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
jellyfin\-hotcache \- manage a safety-oriented local media cache for Jellyfin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jellyfin-hotcache
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jellyfin-hotcache
promotes selected media files from slower storage to a local cache while
keeping Jellyfin's configured media paths stable with symbolic links.
The source-side original is preserved so a cached item can be restored without
copying it back from the cache.
.PP
Normal mutating runs fail closed when active Jellyfin sessions or playback
history cannot be checked. The configured cache root must already exist; the
program will not create a missing cache root because that can conceal a missing
mount.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " FILE
Read configuration from
.IR FILE .
The default is
.IR /etc/jellyfin-hotcache/config.yml .
.TP
.BR \-\-environment-file " " FILE
Read optional environment variables from
.IR FILE .
The default is
.IR /etc/jellyfin-hotcache/environment .
Existing process environment variables take precedence. The file uses simple
.B NAME=value
entries and is not executed as shell code.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Run the read-only preflight and exit. The preflight checks configuration,
Jellyfin API access, playback database connectivity and schema, configured
libraries, cache limits and free space, lock availability, manifest entries,
cache containment, symlink targets, preserved originals, and orphan cache
files. It does not promote, demote, or restore files and does not create the
cache root, lock file, report, or manifest. Filesystem capacity checks
include ZFS dataset quota/refquota information when available.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Force dry-run behavior regardless of the configuration setting.
.TP
.B \-\-no-email
Do not send the run report by email.
.SH CACHE AGING
The
.B cache.hot_window_days
setting determines how recently an item must have been played to continue
qualifying as hot. If
.B cache.enable_demotion
is true,
.B cache.demote_after_days_cold
sets the additional grace period after the item stops qualifying as hot. The
shipped example uses 14 days.
.PP
The older
.B cache.demote_after_days_unwatched
name remains accepted as a compatibility alias. If both names are present,
.B cache.demote_after_days_cold
takes precedence.
.SH FILESYSTEM CAPACITY
Run reports inspect the filesystem containing the cache root. On ZFS, the
report includes the dataset, pool, quota, refquota, used, referenced, available,
and pool free values when the corresponding tools are available.
.PP
The ZFS dataset
.B available
value is used for writable-space reporting. Pool free space is informational.
The report's effective remaining capacity is the smaller of the Hotcache policy
headroom and filesystem headroom after the configured minimum free-space
reserve. Dry-run projected growth is included in that calculation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/jellyfin-hotcache/config.yml
Operator-owned YAML configuration. The Debian package never installs or
overwrites this file.
.TP
.I /etc/jellyfin-hotcache/environment
Optional operator-owned environment file for secrets such as
.B JELLYFIN_API_KEY
and
.BR JELLYFIN_PG_PASSWORD .
It is read automatically by the CLI unless another file is selected.
.TP
.I /usr/share/jellyfin-hotcache/config.yml.example
Package-managed reference configuration.
.TP
.I /run/lock/jellyfin-hotcache.lock
Default run lock path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful normal run, or a preflight with no FAIL results.
.TP
.B 1
One or more operational failures.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration or command setup error. Normal report-delivery failures may also
use this status.
.SH SYSTEMD
The package installs
.B jellyfin-hotcache.service
and
.BR jellyfin-hotcache.timer .
The timer is deliberately not enabled or started on first installation.
Site-specific mount dependencies should be added with a local systemd drop-in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.timer (5),
.BR findmnt (8),
.BR zfs (8),
.BR zpool (8)
